  "name": "PGAA",
  "version": "0.2.1",
  "description": "PGAA is an executable claim-state compiler for perturbation transcriptomics. It combines internal decision state, ranking stability, external evidence, source-data provenance, and branch-specific promotion gates to emit bounded manuscript claim states. Distribution-aware Wasserstein and histogram-shape statistics remain available as upstream scoring modules; they are not claimed as the main methodological novelty.",
